  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cuba: Strengthening local development planning with migration data (Phase II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Whereas detailed demographic information&#x2014;particularly internal migration data&#x2014;is collected in Cuba at the municipal level and is disaggregated by sex, age and territory, it is not always fully utilised in decision-making processes across various levels and sectors. At the same time, the limited use of migration data hampers the development of public policies tailored to specific population groups, such as women and youth, and obstructs the effective management of migration processes and territorial development. Building on the outcomes of a Phase I project, which included the creation of migration indicators and methodological guides to promote the use of migration data, this Phase II project aims to further contribute to good migration governance and sustainable territorial development in Cuba.    To achieve this objective, it is expected that the provincial governments of Pinar del R&#xed;o, Villa Clara and Granma will systematically and gender-sensitively use migration information in the formulation of their Territorial Development Plans (Outcome 1). Specifically, the relevant actors responsible for addressing the demographic dynamics in the provinces of Pinar del R&#xed;o, Villa Clara and Granma will strengthen their technical capacities and have the necessary equipment for the production and management of migration data (Output 1.1); these same actors will increase their knowledge on the use of migration information and data for development decision-making with a gender perspective (Output 1.2); and the coordination mechanisms of the provincial governments of Pinar del R&#xed;o, Clara and Granma will have recommendations and sustainability measures available to effectively manage the migration-development nexus at the territorial level and with a gender approach.</narrative>
  </description>
